  "answer": "The lens maker’s formula is given by 1/f = (n - 1)(1/R1 - 1/R2), where f is the focal length of the lens, n is the refractive index of the lens material, R1 is the radius of curvature of the first surface, and R2 is the radius of curvature of the second surface. This formula helps in calculating the focal length of a lens based on its shape and the refractive index of the material it is made of. The term (n - 1) accounts for the refractive properties of the lens material, while the terms 1/R1 and 1/R2 relate to the curvature of the lens surfaces. The formula is derived from the principles of refraction at curved surfaces and is used to design lenses for various optical applications.",
